// Title: Procdump Execution
// Sigma ID: 2e65275c-8288-4ab4-aeb7-6274f58b6b20
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-08-16 | Modified: 2026-06-29
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1036, T1003.001, credential-access
// Description: Detects usage of the SysInternals Procdump utility
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of procdump by a developer or administrator
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/procdump
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_sysinternals_procdump.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\procdump.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\procdump64.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\procdump64a.exe"
